    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1822">

                <pb facs="1333" n="1217" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1217"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 319.1123L25/18.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Price.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 189.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your Nos. 607
                    and 614 of the 8th and 14th ultimo, relating to the indifference shown by the
                    Panaman authorities to taking any effective steps to redress the wrongs
                    committed in the riots of February 14 last in Panama and on April 2 last in
                    Colon.</p>
                <p>The Department approves your note of September 4 last to the Panaman Foreign
                    Office in reply to its note on the subject and will await the receipt of a
                    response from the Foreign Office to it before giving instructions in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
